      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ارجلهُ</span></b>  <i>He made him to go on foot;</i> (S, K,
TA;) <i>to alight from his beast.</i> (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  And
<i>He granted him some delay,</i> or <i>respite; let him
alone,</i> or <i>left him, for a while.</i> (S, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْجَلْتُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الحِصَانَ فِى الخَيْلِ</span> <i>I sent-the stallion-horse among
the mares.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also 1, in the latter half
of the paragraph, in three places.

